 "answer": "To make a token counter see events across the whole LlamaIndex application, you should assign a `CallbackManager` to the `Settings.callback_manager` attribute. This is outlined in the context provided, specifically in section [6], which describes how to set a global callback manager in LlamaIndex:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core.callbacks import TokenCountingHandler, CallbackManager\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\ntoken_counter = TokenCountingHandler()\nSettings.callback_manager = CallbackManager([token_counter])\n```\n\nBy setting `Settings.callback_manager` to a `CallbackManager` that includes your `TokenCountingHandler`, the token counter will be able to observe and consume events generated throughout the LlamaIndex application.",
